WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.332 --> 00:00:12.075
Anansi the Spider sat in a tall tree, watching Goat work in his garden.

2
00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:16.216
"Goat's melons look delicious!"

3
00:00:16.636 --> 00:00:17.557
thought Anansi.

4
00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:23.218
The spider loved fruit, but he was too lazy to grow anything himself.

5
00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:28.940
When Goat left, Anansi dropped into the garden.

6
00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:32.839
With a thorn, he carved a hole in a melon.

7
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.984
He crawled inside, and began to eat—and eat and eat!

8
00:00:40.145 --> 00:00:42.127
Anansi rubbed his full belly.

9
00:00:42.147 --> 00:00:45.530
"Goat will be back soon," he said.

10
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.051
"I must go."

11
00:00:47.071 --> 00:00:50.595
He tried to crawl out through the hole.

12
00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:53.697
But now he was too fat!

13
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:56.280
"I'll wait until I'm thin again."

14
00:00:57.628 --> 00:00:59.929
Anansi grew bored while he waited.

15
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.272
When Goat returned, Anansi got an idea.

16
00:01:05.232 --> 00:01:08.474
He loved to play tricks—he could trick Goat!

17
00:01:10.955 --> 00:01:12.336
Goat picked up the melon.

18
00:01:12.356 --> 00:01:15.318
"Ow!" Anansi yelped.

19
00:01:15.338 --> 00:01:17.319
"Who said that?"

20
00:01:17.699 --> 00:01:19.500
Goat cried, looking around.

21
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.142
"Me," replied the melon.

22
00:01:24.703 --> 00:01:25.443
Goat blinked.

23
00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:27.204
"Melons can't talk!"

24
00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:29.425
"Yes, we can."

25
00:01:29.445 --> 00:01:32.606
"This is incredible!"

26
00:01:32.906 --> 00:01:33.526
said Goat.

27
00:01:33.546 --> 00:01:36.007
"I must show the queen!"

28
00:01:36.627 --> 00:01:38.168
He hurried toward the palace.

29
00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:41.569
Rattlesnake saw him.

30
00:01:41.589 --> 00:01:43.690
"Where are you going?"

31
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:44.731
she called.

32
00:01:44.751 --> 00:01:49.072
"I'm taking this melon to the queen," replied Goat.

33
00:01:49.092 --> 00:01:50.633
"It talks."

34
00:01:50.653 --> 00:01:52.594
"That's silly."

35
00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:55.855
Rattlesnake laughed.

36
00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:00.113
"As silly as—" "A kind rattlesnake!"

37
00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:01.294
said the melon.

38
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:03.716
Rattlesnake scowled.

39
00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:06.238
"Who said that?"

40
00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.522
"I told you—this melon talks!"

41
00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:11.543
said Goat.

42
00:02:11.563 --> 00:02:14.865
"Amazing!" said Rattlesnake.

43
00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:17.007
"I'll go with you."

44
00:02:18.608 --> 00:02:20.890
Goat and Rattlesnake headed toward the palace.

45
00:02:21.811 --> 00:02:24.073
More animals heard the melon talking.

46
00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.736
They followed Goat and Rattlesnake to the palace.

47
00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:30.272
Goat bowed.

48
00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:34.053
"Your Majesty, we brought you a melon."

49
00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.274
The queen frowned.

50
00:02:36.294 --> 00:02:38.755
"I already have plenty of melons."

51
00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:43.736
"This melon is unique," explained Goat proudly.

52
00:02:43.756 --> 00:02:45.776
"It can talk!"

53
00:02:47.017 --> 00:02:48.557
The queen stepped closer.

54
00:02:48.577 --> 00:02:50.898
"Speak, melon!"

55
00:02:51.258 --> 00:02:51.898
she ordered.

56
00:02:52.718 --> 00:02:54.439
But the melon stayed quiet.

57
00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:59.040
"Melon! I order you to speak!"

58
00:03:00.812 --> 00:03:02.774
Still, the melon was silent.

59
00:03:02.794 --> 00:03:05.156
"What a silly melon!"

60
00:03:05.496 --> 00:03:06.457
the queen snapped.

61
00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:09.860
"Silly?" echoed the melon.

62
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.423
"You're the one who's talking to a melon!"

63
00:03:14.204 --> 00:03:16.566
The queen's face turned bright red.

64
00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:21.570
She picked up the melon and flung it with all her might.

65
00:03:22.972 --> 00:03:27.676
The melon hit a tree in Goat's garden and shattered into pieces.

66
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.841
Anansi crawled out of the melon.

67
00:03:30.861 --> 00:03:33.122
"I'm thin again!"

68
00:03:33.562 --> 00:03:34.543
he said happily.

69
00:03:34.563 --> 00:03:36.364
"I'm hungry too."

70
00:03:36.824 --> 00:03:39.205
He scurried up a nearby banana tree.

71
00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:41.986
Goat returned to his garden.

72
00:03:42.006 --> 00:03:44.647
"Dumb melons!

73
00:03:45.068 --> 00:03:46.788
I'm never listening to you again!"

74
00:03:46.808 --> 00:03:50.410
"Good idea," called a banana.

75
00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.892
"Talking melons always bring trouble!"
